/A 1358 0 R
/Alt (x-y cross-section showing tritium production rate for the pin-cell assembly. Tritium production is zero outside of the breeder regions. Within the breeder regions it follows a smooth gradient with approximate radial symmetry with respect to the central neutron source. There are two peaks with the highest at the outermost radius facing the reflector and the second at the innermost radius facing the neutron source. Values in the breeder regions range from just over one point 4 times 10 to the 8 tallies per second down to approximately 0.4 times 10 to the 8 tallies per second.)
