513 0 obj
<<
/A 1497 0 R
/Alt (Two plots tracing the tritium breeding ratio as a function of trial number for different optimisation strategies over 100 trials. The tritium breeding ratio fluctuates between about 0.1 to 0.8; the baseline 0.723 is noted for reference. Sobol samples are shown on the left and Bayesian optimisation samples are on the right. In the first strategy, a larger proportion of Sobol samples are used and some of these trials exceed the baseline, but there is almost no improvement during Bayesian optimisation. Contrastingly, in the second strategy, a sharp increase is observed at the onset of the Bayesian optimisation sequence; this is followed by a plateau. The best tritium breeding ratios found are 0.793 and 0.802 respectively.)
/K [20 1498 0 R]
/P 137 0 R
/Pg 49 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 6)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
